# ClientAssets/ never holds an original Ultima Online client file.
# Block known stock-client file types and names anywhere in this folder,
# then allowlist specific shard-made files by exact relative path.
# See README.md for the rule this enforces.

*.uop
*.mul
*.idx
*.dll
*.pdb
*.exe
client.exe

# Allowlist: add one line per shard-made file that legitimately carries a
# stock file name or extension. Nothing else under overrides/, cuo-data/
# or plugins/ can be tracked until it is listed here explicitly.
# Example (uncomment when the shard actually ships a hues.mul override):
# !/overrides/hues.mul

# The BSD 2-Clause notice must ship with the client binaries. This is the
# one file under client/ that is shard-tracked; ClassicUO.exe, cuo.dll and
# every other client binary stay untracked, same as ShardPlugin.dll.
!/client/LICENSE.md

!.gitkeep
!README.md
!.gitignore
